* Lab 13-10 -- a cavity resonator near its TE101 mode as a parallel RLC (Example 13-10.5).
* Near one resonance a cavity's input behaves like a parallel RLC with the same f0 and Q. With R = 1 kohm,
* f0 = 9.2732 GHz and Q = 7838: C = Q/(2 pi f0 R) = 134.52 pF and L = 1/((2 pi f0)^2 C) = 2.1898 pH.
* A 1 mA AC current drives the tank; the half-power points give the bandwidth, and their geometric mean is f0
* (exact for a parallel RLC).
*
* EXPECT f0 key:../../chapters/13-10-waveguides-and-resonators.md#Sim_13-10.a scale=1e9 rtol=1e-5
* EXPECT q key:../../chapters/13-10-waveguides-and-resonators.md#Sim_13-10.b rtol=2e-3

IIN 0 tank DC 0 AC 1m
RT tank 0 1k
CT tank 0 134.519p
LT tank 0 2.18983p

.control
ac lin 20001 9.2652e9 9.2812e9
let mag = abs(v(tank))
meas ac vpk max mag
let lvl = vpk / sqrt(2)
meas ac flo when mag=lvl rise=1
meas ac fhi when mag=lvl fall=1
let f0 = sqrt(flo * fhi)
let q = f0 / (fhi - flo)
print f0 q
quit
.endc
.end
